  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1054 PM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nUpper ridging will largely dominate the eastern CONUS to start the \nweekend; however, a cutoff low further develops off the east coast of\nFlorida and slowly makes its way northeast through early next week. \nMeanwhile, a shortwave trough looks to traverse the Mississippi \nRiver Valley but weaken as it progresses farther east over the \nTennessee Valley Sunday night into Monday. Upper ridging will then \ntake hold Monday into Tuesday. At the surface, high pressure over the\neastern US will be pushed east through the weekend as a cold front \nsweeps over the Mississippi River Valley. This feature is then shown\nto move over the region Sunday into Monday, with high pressure \npushing southward from Canada by Tuesday. \n\nOverall, the weather pattern stays fairly dry. The main time window \nof any precipitation potential is Sunday into Monday with frontal \npassage. However, the question will be whether enough moisture \nremains/is realized with FROPA for showers to occur. This will be \nmonitored. As for temperatures, expect highs in the upper 60s to \nlower 70s on Saturday to drop into the mid 50s to lower 60s by \nTuesday. Lows will follow a similar pattern, beginning in the mid 40s\nto lower 50s Friday night and dropping into the 30s once again by \nMonday night.",
